      },
      "shell": "/usr/bin/osascript -l JavaScript -e 'var s = $.NSUserDefaults.alloc.initWithSuiteName(\"com.apple.applicationaccess\"); (ObjC.unwrap(s.objectForKey(\"allowCloudDesktopAndDocuments\")) == false && s.objectIsForcedForKey(\"allowCloudDesktopAndDocuments\")) ? \"PASS\" : \"FAIL\"'"
    }
  },
  "discussion": "The macOS system's ability to automatically synchronize a user's desktop and documents folder to their iCloud Drive _MUST_ be disabled, unless the organization has explicitly authorized the use of iCloud as a approved file management service.\n\nApple's iCloud service does not provide an organization with enough control over the storage and access of data and, therefore, automated file synchronization _MUST_ be controlled by an organization approved service.\n\nThis requirement helps ensure that organizational file data is managed in accordance with established security, privacy, access-control, and data governance requirements.\n",
  "id": "mscp.icloud_sync_disable",
